{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:e417b7a78a91fd24","name":"The Madness of Knowledge","source":{"id":"source:reference-e417b7a78a91fd24","title":"The Madness of Knowledge","revision":20552,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T00:04:24Z","sha256":"43ce0f0a549e64574d9780d56784f8a3099779d49a292d38008158305c52d6cc","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=20552","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=The%20Madness%20of%20Knowledge&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-e417b7a78a91fd24","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi Academy Training Manual"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi_Academy_Training_Manual"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Before ",{"tag":"a","children":["Holocron"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Holocron"}," technology was developed, and sometimes even after, ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Sith"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Sith","referenceId":"reference:32bde5e69837ac8e"}," recorded much of their dark knowledge in traditional forms. Locked away in the mausoleums dedicated to ancient Sith Lords are thousands of scrolls, tomes, and tablets bearing instructions on how to master a variety of Sith techniques. Like ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Holocrons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Holocrons"},", these ancient writings describe the methods of using lost [",{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Dark Side"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dark_Side"}]},"] ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Powers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Powers","referenceId":"reference:85acec94cd1ca5f3"},", the construction of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Weapons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Weapons"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Artifacts"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Artifacts"},", information on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Alchemy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Alchemy"},", and treaties on the domination and destruction of others. \n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Sith scrolls, tomes, and tablets function in much the same way as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Holocron"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Holocron"}," for the purposes of learning new ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Powers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Powers","referenceId":"reference:85acec94cd1ca5f3"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Talents"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Talents"},". However, these writing have neither a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi Master Holocron Gatekeeper"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi_Master_Holocron_Gatekeeper","referenceId":"reference:5a76dfeecca62d2e"}," nor a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Lord Holocron Gatekeeper"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Lord_Holocron_Gatekeeper","referenceId":"reference:6520155ab5b3e0a6"},", and as such their knowledge is open to anyone who can master them, given time. Searchers should beware; many Sith writings are imbued with the madness of their creators, and the knowledge they contain has been known to drive the unprepared student to insanity.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["The Madness of Knowledge Statistics (CL 6)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Trigger:"]}," A creature reads an ancient Sith tome, scroll, or tablet.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Attack:"]}," +8 vs ",{"tag":"a","children":["Will Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Will_Defense"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Damage:"]}," - (-2 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Persistent"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Persistent"}," steps on the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Condition Track"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Condition_Track"},"; -5 penalty to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Will Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Will_Defense"},")\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Recurrence:"]}," None.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Suggested ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skills"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skills","referenceId":"reference:66d0f523a379b2de"},":"]}," The following are suggested ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skills"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skills","referenceId":"reference:66d0f523a379b2de"}," for this Hazard:\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Treat Injury"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Treat_Injury","referenceId":"reference:f1b9875c2302ce61"}," (DC 25):"]}," The character treats The Madness of Knowledge along with 8 hours of rest (cannot be performed by the victim)."]}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Special:"]}," The character is filled with paranoia and creeping insanity until treated, and any time the character rolls a Natural 1 on an attack roll, their next attack roll made before the end of the encounter must be against an ally, not an enemy.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
